# Next.js App Router

## Pages And Layouts

- Keep route files thin. `page.tsx` and `layout.tsx` compose sections from `src/modules` or `src/shared`; they do not contain large UI or business logic.
- Name route components `Page`, `Layout`, `Loading`, `Error`, `GlobalError`, or `NotFound`.
- Use Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only when the file needs state, effects, event handlers, browser APIs, or client-only hooks.
- Split complex pages into clear sections/components under the relevant `src/modules/<feature>/components` folder.

## Special Files

- `error.tsx` and `global-error.tsx` are Client Components that receive `{ error, retry }` (Next.js 16.4 — not `reset`). Reuse `ErrorFallback` from `src/shared/components/error-fallback.tsx`.
- `global-error.tsx` renders its own `<html>`/`<body>` and must import `globals.css` itself.
- `not-found.tsx` handles unknown routes and `notFound()` calls; mark it `robots: { index: false }`.
- Add a segment-level `loading.tsx` / `error.tsx` when a route has its own data and failure modes.
- `src/proxy.ts` (formerly middleware) runs only on paths in its `matcher`. Keep static assets, `_next`, and metadata files excluded, and keep it free of auth cookie reads.

## Data And Rendering

- Fetch server-side data through the owning resource's `server.ts` (in `src/modules/<feature>/api/`, or `src/shared/api/<resource>/` when shared), not with raw `fetch` inside route files.
- Keep route-level fetching unauthenticated and cookie-free so pages stay SSG/ISR-capable. Authenticated data belongs in client components via React Query.
- Avoid client fetching in route components unless the UX requires client state or live interactions. When a client component needs server-warmed data, prefetch with `getQueryClient()` and hydrate with `HydrationBoundary`.
- Cache Components is disabled: do not export `instant` or use `"use cache"`. Use `export const revalidate = <seconds>` or per-request `revalidate`/`tags` instead.
- For dynamic segments, use `generateStaticParams` + `revalidate` (ISR) for public pages, and call `notFound()` when `isNotFoundError(error)`.
- Render mode, freshness, and metadata are covered in `performance-seo`.

## Navigation

- Use `next/link` for internal navigation and `ROUTES` from `src/shared/constants/routes.ts` for paths. Add an entry when a new top-level route is introduced; use a function for dynamic routes (``detail: (slug: string) => `/properties/${slug}` ``).

## Tooling

- The Next.js DevTools MCP (`next-devtools`, configured in `.mcp.json` / `.cursor/mcp.json`) and the bundled docs in `node_modules/next/dist/docs` are the source of truth for framework APIs.
